    "narrative": "For May 23, 2026, Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily into high-upside matchups against mediocre arms. **Corbin Carroll** (81.41) leads the charge as our strongest play, bolstered by a plus-matchup against Michael Lorenzen and strong projected xwOBA figures. He is flanked by **Tyler Soderstrom** (73.03) and **James Wood** (70.10), both of whom capitalize on soft SP_xERA matchups against Lucas Giolito and Grant Holmes, respectively. **Brice Turang** (72.43) remains a high-floor start against Roki Sasaki; despite Sasaki\u2019s pedigree, the current metrics suggest a favorable environment for **Brice Turang** to utilize his speed\u2014a crucial factor given our emphasis on stolen bases.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Kyle Karros** (51.91), who hovered near the bottom of our starting threshold but ultimately fell short due to a stagnant lineup spot and a lack of comparative platoon advantage versus the rest of our utility options. Conversely, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (60.32) was cleared for the starting lineup despite a difficult matchup against George Kirby, largely because his elite dynamic platoon data offset the SP\u2019s high skill level. We are tracking a few risks: **Jose Caballero** remains sidelined due to a rainout, and **Mickey Moniak** continues to occupy an IL slot. With all other starters pending official confirmation, our aggressive baseline reliance on players like **Dalton Rushing** and **Cole Young** assumes standard lineup placement; should their actual spots shift downward, their marginal scores (48.28 and 47.86) indicate they remain the first candidates for benching to preserve our game caps.",
